     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>HI Everyone,<div><br></div><div>i have a need to user R and connect ot my hortonworks hdfs for the analytics. I  am new to R and starting my journey from this task to R. Based on my understanding i we can install R on any remote server and use it through putty on any machine. Or install Rstudio server on any remote  machine and use it through web browser. This looks good to me. </div><div><br></div><div>Now the problem starts : I want to install RHadoop with my hadoop cluster. </div><div><br></div><div>The guide says to install below. How to install this. On which node to install Rstudio if i want to use as web. Shall i install R Studio on namenode or datanode. or on ll the node.</div><div><br></div><div>Please look this link for more detail :<a href=\"https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/Installing-RHadoop-on-RHEL\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/Installing-RHadoop-on-RHEL&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490318366000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1uUK6W70-Yn6fJjUwWSk4z\">https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/Installing-RHadoop-on-RHEL</a> </div><div><br></div><div><table style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-collapse:collapse;display:block;width:700px;overflow:auto;word-break:keep-all;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Arial,freesans,sans-serif,&#39;Apple Color Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Symbol&#39;;font-size:16px;line-height:25.6px\"><thead style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><th style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;font-weight:bold;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\">Package</th><th style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;font-weight:bold;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\">Where to Install</th></tr></thead><tbody style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;padding-top:0.2em;padding-bottom:0.2em;border-radius:3px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157)\">plyrmr</code></td><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\">On <strong style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">every node</strong> in the cluster</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204);background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;padding-top:0.2em;padding-bottom:0.2em;border-radius:3px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157)\">ravro</code></td><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\">Only on the node that runs the R client</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;padding-top:0.2em;padding-bottom:0.2em;border-radius:3px;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.0392157)\">rhbase</code></td><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid rgb(221,221,221)\">Only on the node that runs the R client</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-top-width:1px;border-top-style:solid;border-top-color:rgb(204,204,204);background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><td style=\"box